            <ArticleTitle>Mycotic aneurysm of left anterior descending artery after sirolimus-eluting stent implantation: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>282-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of mycotic aneurysms due to Staphylococcus aureus infection in the left anterior descending coronary artery in a 56-year-old male after implantation of a sirolimus-eluting stent. This is an unreported complication of a drug-eluting stent.</AbstractText>
